#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""
rush-autopilot — deterministic planner for Rush LiveDev benchmark campaigns.

Reads repo state (VERSION, git HEAD, milestones, evidence tree, benchmark plans)
and hardware state (real or fake sysfs) to produce a typed Plan of PlanSteps.
The planner is DETERMINISTIC: the same inputs always produce the same Plan.
No AI calls. No network. No real hardware required (use --fake-sys for tests).

Usage:
  tools/rush-autopilot plan --auto
  tools/rush-autopilot plan --dry-run
  tools/rush-autopilot plan --slot laptop
  tools/rush-autopilot plan --slot desktop
  tools/rush-autopilot plan --output <path>
  tools/rush-autopilot plan --repo <path>
  tools/rush-autopilot plan --fake-sys <path>

The plan subcommand is the only subcommand in this phase. Future phases may
add 'execute' and 'resume' subcommands.

Plan output (JSON):
  {
    "schema_version": 1,
    "plan_kind": "rush-autopilot-plan",
    "generated_at": "<ISO 8601 UTC — from context, not wall clock>",
    "source_version": "<from VERSION>",
    "source_commit": "<40-char git SHA>",
    "repo_root": "<path>",
    "hardware_slot": "laptop" | "desktop" | "server" | "realtime-capable" | "ambiguous",
    "slot_confidence": "high" | "medium" | "low",
    "ambiguities": ["..."],
    "open_criteria": [{"milestone": "0.6.0-beta.1", "criterion": "...", "requires_slot": "laptop"}],
    "existing_evidence": ["host-bench/2026-06-10-victus/"],
    "steps": [
      {
        "seq": 0,
        "kind": "physical-prompt" | "command" | "validation",
        "default": "wait" | "proceed" | "skip" | "ask" | "abort",
        "reason": "...",
        "rollback": "...",
        # for kind=command:
        "argv": ["rush-exec", "--run-dir", "...", "--", "rushbench", "run", ...],
        # for kind=physical-prompt:
        "action": "...",
        "detection_signal": "...",
        "timeout": "5m" | "10m",
        # for kind=validation:
        "validator": "validate-hwtest-evidence.py",
        "bundle": "<path>"
      }
    ]
  }

Human-facing rule (docs/automation-human-interface.md §5):
  Do not ask the user for anything derivable from repo or hardware state.
  If ambiguous, report the ambiguity and choose a safe default.

Exit codes:
  0 — plan generated successfully
  1 — cannot generate plan (missing milestones file, no open criteria, etc.)
  2 — internal error
"""

